A subsequence is **increasing** if the values are strictly increasing:

i < j implies x_{indices(i)} < x_{indices(j)}

Formally: StrictMono (seq ∘ sub.indices).

A subsequence is **decreasing** if values are strictly decreasing:

i < j implies x_{indices(i)} > x_{indices(j)}

Note: strictly decreasing, not just non-increasing.
